/ref 1074 "Because $f$ is $10$-periodic on $[-5,5]$, we have $L=5$, so Fourier series on this interval use the basis \n\n$$\ncos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})\\,\\text{and}\\,sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5}).\n$$\n\nNext, since $f$ is odd, its Fourier series contains only sine terms. For a second-order equation with no ${y}^{′}$ (damping) term, the particular solution inherits this property and is also an odd function.\n\nTherefore, the appropriate form for ${y}_{p}$ is a sine series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372861 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372862 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372861 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372863 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372861 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372864 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372861 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372865 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372861 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372861 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372861 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186372864 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372861 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f04ef90f-3003-58fb-a7fe-77d398fbdee2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372862 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{10})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372862 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372862 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fe92f4fa-7615-54d2-a819-127fb1a673f2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372863 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{10})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372863 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372863 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3b55cc73-4e32-591c-bee5-a9d934861abd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372864 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921863728